pplicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORIKOSHI HIROMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MOCHIZUKI NOBUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIINOKI YASUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA SEIICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UMEDA NOBUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA HIROKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIKOSHI, HIROMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOCHIZUKI, NOBUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIINOKI, YASUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA, SEIICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UMEDA, NOBUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Thieno[2,3-d]pyrimidine compounds of general formula (1) useful as drugs having a cGMP-specific phosphodiesterase inhibiting effect and so on; and a process for the preparation of the same wherein Q is a group represented by the general formula: (CH2)n-N(r1)-C(r2)(r3), CH=CH-CH=CH, or (CH2)m which is bonded to a and b; R1 is hydrogen or C1-C6 alkyl; R2 is C3-C8 cycloalkyl optionally substituted with G1, phenyl optionally substituted with G2, or a saturated or unsaturated heterocyclic group having 1 to 4 heteroatoms selected from among N, O and S and being optionally substituted with G3; and R3 is a saturated or unsaturated heterocyclic group having 1 to 4 heteroatoms selected from among N, O and S and being optionally substituted with G3 or a group represented by the general formula: (CH2)kC(=O)R4 or CH=CHC(O)R4.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des composés de thiéno[2,3-d]pyrimidine de la formule générale (1), qui sont utiles en tant que médicaments ayant un effet d'inhibition de la phosphodiestérase spécifique au cGMP, etc., et un procédé de préparation desdits composés. Dans ladite formule, Q est un groupe de la formule générale (CH2)n-N(r1)-C(r2)(r3), CH=CH-CH=CH, ou (CH2)m lequel est lié à a et b; R1 est hydrogène ou alkyle C1-C6; R2 est cycloalkyle C3-C8 éventuellement substitué par G1, phényle éventuellement substitué par G2, ou un groupe hétérocyclique saturé ou insaturé comprenant 1 à 4 hétéroatomes choisis entre N, O et S et éventuellement substitué par G3 ou un groupe de la formule générale (CH2)kC(=O)R4 ou CH=CHC(O)R4.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>